{"version":1,"key":"card:651","content":{"id":651,"content":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"破窗效应是犯罪心理学上一个著名的理论：如果对环境中的一个小问题不及时修复，这个小问题就会暗示此处环境没人管，从而造成更大的混乱。"}],"disableDrag":false},{"type":"paragraph","disableDrag":false,"children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"在 1982 年三月的《大西洋周刊》上，犯罪心理学家詹姆斯·Q·威尔逊及乔治·凯林发表了一片《Broken Window》的文章，两位作者为了阐述无序的环境会导致犯罪，举了一个例子："}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","disableDrag":false,"children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"试想一幢建筑，如果有一扇窗户破了（Broken Window），且迟迟没有人去修补。路人看到后就会觉得：这里没人管，没人负责。"}]},{"type":"paragraph","disableDrag":false,"children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"很快，其他的窗户也会被打破。既然没人管，那么哪怕是打破更多的窗户、甚至闯入建筑内搞破坏，也不会受惩罚。这扇没人修的「破窗」，就是混乱的开始。"}]}]},{"type":"image","url":"http://blog-hostimaging.oss-cn-beijing.aliyuncs.com/image_e7b46637-7046-4820-b447-b6f2cd0dc1f6.webp","uuid":"a0d4cd5a-19b9-43b6-aaee-9de6ca5da98b","pasteUploading":false,"children":[{"type":"formatted","text":""}],"previewUrl":"http://blog-hostimaging.oss-cn-beijing.aliyuncs.com/image_e7b46637-7046-4820-b447-b6f2cd0dc1f6.webp","width":701.0848473108825},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"由于这个比喻深入人心，因此大家就用破窗效应（Broken Window Theory）来指代这一套理论。"}],"disableDrag":false},{"type":"paragraph","disableDrag":false,"children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"在我们的生活中也经常会看到一些破窗效应："}]},{"type":"bulleted-list","children":[{"type":"list-item","children":[{"type":"paragraph","disableDrag":false,"children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"为了减肥你每天都进行运动，突然有一天下雨，你中断了（破窗），第二天没有及时补上，你心理就会想，反正都中断了，不如歇一天吧，最终会导致彻底放弃"}]}]},{"type":"list-item","children":[{"type":"paragraph","disableDrag":false,"children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"家里卫生本来很干净，只有偷懒一次，桌子上的易拉罐、卫生纸没有及时清理（破窗），那么就会暗示你可以不整理卫生，导致垃圾越堆越多，成为垃圾堆"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","disableDrag":false,"children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"破窗效应给我们带来的启示就是"},{"type":"formatted","text":"防微杜渐","bold":true},{"type":"formatted","text":"："}]},{"type":"bulleted-list","children":[{"type":"list-item","children":[{"type":"paragraph","disableDrag":false,"children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"对于管理者/家长：当看到第一扇窗被打破时（员工迟到、孩子撒谎），要及时进行修补，表明态度"}]}]},{"type":"list-item","children":[{"type":"paragraph","disableDrag":false,"children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"对于个人：不要轻易打破第一扇窗，不要想着「仅此一次，下不为例」，这一次往往就是溃败的开始，"},{"type":"content-link","contentId":4900,"contentType":"card","contentTitle":"","refId":649,"children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"就像是在滑梯顶端迈出的一步"}]},{"type":"formatted","text":"，一旦迈出，就会随着重力沿着滑梯不断下降，直至走向彻底的混乱"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","disableDrag":false,"children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"参考："}]},{"type":"bulleted-list","children":[{"type":"list-item","children":[{"type":"paragraph","disableDrag":false,"children":[{"text":"","type":"formatted"},{"type":"link","url":"https://zh.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E7%A0%B4%E7%AA%97%E6%95%88%E5%BA%94","openEdit":false,"children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"破窗效应"}]},{"text":"","type":"formatted"}]}]}]}],"tags":["心理学/破窗效应"],"createTime":1767143210066,"updateTime":1777355948261,"linkedCards":[]},"meta":{"type":"card","publishTime":1777355948261},"links":{"card:649":{"key":"card:649","type":"card","id":649}}}